    "mechanism": "Sustained aggressor direction: a single last-trade aggressor read is noisy (one snapshot can be an isolated fill), so the trailing-30s mean of the signed gap aggregates whether the recent prints have been consistently buyer- or seller-initiated. Persistent net buyer aggression over 30s means demand is repeatedly crossing to pay up -- informed buying that has not yet been absorbed -- and predicts short-horizon upward continuation; persistent seller aggression is the mirror. Magnitude-weighted (wide-quote aggression counts more), unlike the pure sign-frequency variant.",
